.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt LIBTRACECMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tracecmp_open ,
.Nm tracecmp_stats ,
.Nm tracecmp_dtrace_open
.Nd explicitly authorized DTrace descriptor delegation
.Sh LIBRARY
.Li libtracecmp
.Pq Fl ltracecmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In tracecmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn tracecmp_open "int *dtracefd"
.Ft int
.Fn tracecmp_stats "struct tracecmp_stats *stats"
.Ft dtrace_hdl_t *
.Fn tracecmp_dtrace_open "int flags" "int *errp"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn tracecmp_open
connects to the global
.Dq system.Trace
service through
.Xr libservice 3 ,
negotiates version 1.0.0, and requests one DTrace consumer descriptor.
Applications do not supply a component or provider name.
.Pp
.Fn tracecmp_dtrace_open
is the normal application interface.
It requests the delegated descriptor, constructs a
.Xr libdtrace 3
handle with
.Fn dtrace_fdopen ,
and closes the intermediate descriptor.
The descriptor constructor duplicates its input, so the caller retains
ownership on both success and failure.
The
.Dv DTRACE_O_NODEV
flag is rejected because a delegated consumer is the purpose of this API.
.Pp
The constructor configures automatic buffer resizing, switch buffers, and a
250 millisecond switch rate.
Principal and aggregation buffer sizes scale with physical RAM and online CPU
count and are capped at 32 MiB per CPU; dynamic-variable storage is capped at
64 MiB.
On systems where topology cannot be queried, the fallback is 4 MiB.
Applications may call
.Fn dtrace_setopt
before enabling probes to replace these defaults.
.Fn tracecmp_open
is the lower-level interface for consumers that deliberately manage the raw
descriptor.
.Pp
.Fn tracecmp_stats
retrieves the provider's operational counters into
.Fa stats
without delegating a descriptor.
The
.Vt struct tracecmp_stats
reports the number of DTrace consumer descriptors the provider has
.Va opened
and the number of requests it has
.Va rejected .
It returns zero on success and \-1 on failure with
.Va errno
set.
.Pp
The provider advertises the raw-descriptor feature only for a client label
listed explicitly in
.Pa /etc/traced.allow .
Unlisted clients receive
.Er EACCES .
Such a descriptor must have a complete DTrace ioctl allowlist, be
transferable only for its initial delivery, and be closed on fork and exec.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtrace 1 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr traced 8
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Capsicum rights and ioctl lists cannot express D language probe, predicate,
or action policy.
A future broker-owned session API should be preferred for untrusted tracing
programs.
